---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

/**
 * This section is the one place the full technical range is stated. Keep the
 * hero and section leads free of capability lists so nothing repeats.
 *
 * Photo is picked up automatically. Drop a file at `src/assets/profile.jpg`
 * (.jpeg, .png and .webp also work) and it appears; with no file present the
 * text runs full width.
 */
const matches = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>(
  '../assets/profile.{jpg,jpeg,png,webp}',
  { eager: true }
);
const photo = Object.values(matches)[0]?.default;
---

<div class:list={['about', photo && 'about--with-photo']}>
  {
    photo && (
      <div class="about__photo">
        <Image src={photo} alt={SITE.name} widths={[240, 480]} loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    )
  }

  <div class="about__text">
    <p>
      Hi, I'm Theodor, a Unity developer and architect based in Romania, with 14 years building
      games across PC, mobile, TVs and VR.
    </p>

    <p>
      Much of my work sits in the areas of a game that players never see. Real-time and turn-based
      multiplayer, network communication and optimisation, and server-authoritative designs that
      keep the server the source of truth so clients cannot manipulate outcomes. Around that, system
      design grounded in established patterns and coding principles, and building, extending or
      adapting the plugins and frameworks a team depends on.
    </p>

    <p>
      I've spent as many years on the operational side: feature flagging, phased rollouts, A/B
      testing, content updates and tuning. Shipping is the beginning of the work rather than the end of it.
      I care as much about the codebase as the people building it, and whether I'm leading a team or
      embedded as a contributor, I bring the same focus on solid architecture, clear communication
      and genuine ownership of what ships.
    </p>

    <p>
      More recently, AI tools like Claude Code have become a core part of how I work, helping me
      plan better, catch issues earlier, and think problems through before writing a line of code.
    </p>

    <p>
      Outside of work I've spent more hours than I can count in the game worlds I grew up loving,
      probably part of why this industry still feels endlessly interesting. Always up for a
      conversation about game architecture, multiplayer systems, or where AI-assisted development
      goes next.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .about--with-photo {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 13rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .about__photo :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .about__text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .about--with-photo {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .about__photo {
      max-width: 10rem;
    }
  }
</style>
